# CoX room agents — no clobbering siblings

**Non-negotiable.** Parallel CoX room agents share one checkout
(`OSRS-Content/`, `test/raids/`, `docs/minigames/cox/`). Your room lane must
**never** move, reset, or overwrite another room's work to green a gate.

## Forbidden

- **Any branch switch**: `git checkout`, `git switch`, `git checkout -b`
  (except the one-time create of your own `cursor/cox-<room>-*-da39` at
  start), detached HEAD, or hopping to `v3` / `cursor/cox-raid-rooms-da39`
  / a sibling room branch mid-work
- `git checkout -f`, `git reset --hard`, or `git clean` on the shared parent
  or on `OSRS-Content/` (wipes sibling WIP)
- `git stash` / `stash drop` of files you do not own
- Replacing another room's `test/raids/cox_<other>.lua` (including
  `cp`, `sed -i`, hardlink games, or "restore from pin")
- Rewriting `cox.constant` / `cox.varp` / `cox.npc` / shared `cox_*.rs2`
  except **additive** `^cox_<your_room>_…` / `%cox_<your_room>_…` blocks
- Editing `cox_layout.rs2`, `cox.rs2` (except a marked `::coxrun` for your
  room), `cox_points.rs2`, or a sibling room's `cox_<sibling>.rs2`
- Renaming or moving trees to `*.skip`, `/tmp`, or "park" backups (also
  covered by `no-park-sibling-content`)
- Pointing the `OSRS-Content` submodule gitlink at a commit that drops
  sibling room changes you did not author
- Running `prepare_scripts.py` / pack rebuilds that you then "fix" by
  restoring a private copy of **another** room's harness
- Background watchers that rewrite sibling files on a timer
- `cp` of `/opt/cursor/artifacts/*.owned` (or any pin) over the live tree
- `run.py … --rebuild-scripts` while siblings may be mid-gate on the same
  checkout (use `--no-build` + private `QUEST_BINARY` only)
- Starting a gate while another room already holds `/tmp/cox_raid_gate.lock`
  or `/tmp/raid_gate.lock` — wait; do not race with a second flock name

## Required

- **One branch for life of the lane.** Create `cursor/cox-<room>-*-da39`
  once from the parent base, push it, and **never leave it**. All commits,
  gates, and PRs stay on that branch.
- Edit only the ownership table row in `docs/minigames/cox/ROOM_AGENT.md`
- If `docs/minigames/cox/agent_briefs/AGENTS.md` says **HARD STOP**: idle
  with zero edits until parent unfreezes your room by name
- Shared file edits: take the named flock (`/tmp/cox_config.lock`,
  `/tmp/cox_puzzles.lock`, `/tmp/cox_minions.lock`, …), touch only your
  symbols, release
- Gate with `QUEST_BINARY` private to your room when possible; use
  `--no-build` if a sibling holds the pack lock — do not rebuild by
  deleting their tree
- If a sibling file is broken: **report it**, do not rewrite or park it

See `docs/minigames/cox/ROOM_AGENT.md` § Standing rules and
`docs/minigames/cox/agent_briefs/AGENTS.md`.
